speechtext:
The amendment is really that clause 1, instead of being as it is in the Bill, should be as the hon. member has read it. But, as I stated, the intention was that clause 1 of the Bill should become clause 2, and I mentioned that. The amendment is simply that clause 1 should read as follows;
Paragraph A, of section 9, of chapter 52w of the statute of 1893, is hereby repealed.
But as the hon. member stated that the present clause 1 would become clause 2, I thought in explanation in committee I was justified in mentioning it.
